<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Dilemmas tied to the time of year, or to the aftermath of a raid. -->

  <!-- ===================== Midsummer ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Council_Dilemma_Midsummer</defName>
    <label>midsummer night</label>
    <weight>0.8</weight>
    <cooldownDays>50</cooldownDays>
    <seasons><li>Summer</li><li>PermanentSummer</li></seasons>
    <texts>
      <li>It's the shortest night of the year, and {A_nameDef} wants a bonfire, a proper one taller than the roof, with singing and drinking and the night shift let off for once.\n\nIt would burn through a good stack of firewood.</li>
      <li>{A_nameDef} has spent a week stacking logs behind the barn for midsummer, and has finally asked the council for permission to light them.</li>
    </texts>
    <traditionOption>0</traditionOption>
    <traditionLabel>the midsummer bonfire</traditionLabel>
    <defaultOption>1</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>Light the bonfire</label>
        <outcome>The midsummer fire burned until dawn, and most of the colony was still around it when the sun came up.</outcome>
        <ways><tradition>4</tradition><toil>-5</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Consume"><what>WoodLog</what><count>40</count></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Bonfire</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Pyre</thought><onlyTrait><li>Pyromaniac</li></onlyTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>5</amount></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Standards"><target>Colony</target><amount>0.03</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Save the wood this year</label>
        <outcome>No bonfire. {A_nameDef} sat on the log pile all evening, looking at it.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>-3</generosity><toil>4</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_NoCelebration</thought><exceptTrait><li>Ascetic</li></exceptTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>-3</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>A small fire, no drinking</label>
        <outcome>They had a small fire and went to bed early. {A_nameDef} called it "a candle with ambitions."</outcome>
        <ways><tradition>2</tradition><toil>2</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Consume"><what>WoodLog</what><count>12</count></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Stories</thought></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

  <!-- ===================== Harvest home ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Council_Dilemma_HarvestHome</defName>
    <label>harvest home</label>
    <workerClass>ColonyCouncil.DilemmaWorker_Feast</workerClass>
    <weight>0.8</weight>
    <cooldownDays>50</cooldownDays>
    <seasons><li>Fall</li></seasons>
    <roleA>
      <passion>Plants</passion>
    </roleA>
    <thingCount>25</thingCount>
    <texts>
      <li>The last of the crops are in. {A_nameDef}, who planted most of them, wants a harvest supper with second helpings for everyone. It would cost about {COUNT} raw food.\n\nThe stores will have to last the winter either way.</li>
      <li>{A_nameDef} has spent the whole season in the fields and is asking for one night to celebrate, a harvest home costing about {COUNT} raw food. "We grew it," {A_nameDef} says. "We should get to taste it."</li>
    </texts>
    <traditionOption>0</traditionOption>
    <traditionLabel>harvest home</traditionLabel>
    <defaultOption>1</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>A harvest feast for everyone</label>
        <outcome>The harvest home went on late, and even the cook had seconds.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>5</generosity><tradition>4</tradition><toil>-3</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Consume"><what>rawfood</what></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_HarvestHome</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>6</amount></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Standards"><target>Colony</target><amount>0.04</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Store every scrap for winter</label>
        <outcome>Every grain went into storage for the winter. {A_nameDef} thinks a season's work deserved better.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>-5</generosity><toil>3</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_NoCelebration</thought><exceptTrait><li>Ascetic</li></exceptTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_Dlm_FeastDenied</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>-4</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>A modest supper</label>
        <outcome>They had a good meal, nothing extravagant, and the stores hardly felt it.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>2</generosity></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Consume"><what>rawfood</what><count>10</count></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_SmallFeast</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>2</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

  <!-- ===================== Midwinter ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Council_Dilemma_Midwinter</defName>
    <label>the longest night</label>
    <weight>0.8</weight>
    <cooldownDays>50</cooldownDays>
    <seasons><li>Winter</li><li>PermanentWinter</li></seasons>
    <texts>
      <li>It's the longest night of the year, dark by mid-afternoon and bitterly cold. {A_nameDef} thinks the colony should mark it the way people did back home, with extra food and a long evening around the fire.</li>
      <li>Last night {A_nameDef} found the colonists huddled in separate rooms, each alone with the cold. "It's midwinter," {A_nameDef} told the council. "We should be together for it."</li>
    </texts>
    <traditionOption>0</traditionOption>
    <traditionLabel>the midwinter supper</traditionLabel>
    <defaultOption>2</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>Extra rations for the long night</label>
        <outcome>The colony ate well on the longest night, and there was singing afterward.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>4</generosity><tradition>4</tradition><toil>-2</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Consume"><what>rawfood</what><count>20</count></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Midwinter</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>4</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Stories by the fire, no feast</label>
        <outcome>They spent the evening telling stories around the fire, some sad, some filthy, until the fire burned down.</outcome>
        <ways><tradition>4</tradition></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Stories</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>2</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Just another night</label>
        <outcome>The longest night passed like any other, cold and dark and quiet.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>-2</generosity><tradition>-4</tradition></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_NoCelebration</thought><exceptTrait><li>Ascetic</li><li>Psychopath</li></exceptTrait></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

  <!-- ===================== Naming the year ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Council_Dilemma_NameTheYear</defName>
    <label>naming the year</label>
    <weight>0.6</weight>
    <cooldownDays>55</cooldownDays>
    <seasons><li>Spring</li></seasons>
    <roleA>
      <notTrait><li>Ascetic</li></notTrait>
    </roleA>
    <texts>
      <li>It started as a joke at dinner, the idea that the new year needs a name, and now the colony is arguing about it. {A_nameDef} has proposed "the year of {A_nameDef}," loudly and often.\n\nThe council has been asked to settle it.</li>
      <li>Someone decided the annals need a name for the new year. {A_nameDef} has put forward {A_possessive} own name, with a straight face. Others want to name it for the colony's dead, and one person keeps suggesting the muffalo.</li>
    </texts>
    <traditionOption>2</traditionOption>
    <traditionLabel>naming the year after a muffalo</traditionLabel>
    <defaultOption>2</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>The year of {A_nameDef}</label>
        <outcome>This is now officially the year of {A_nameDef}. {A_nameDef} has mentioned it a dozen times since breakfast.</outcome>
        <ways><tradition>-4</tradition></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_Dlm_NamedYear</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>6</amount></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Vanity</thought><onlyTrait><li>Jealous</li><li>Greedy</li><li>Abrasive</li></onlyTrait></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Name it for those we lost</label>
        <outcome>The year carries the names of the dead, and the arguing stopped.</outcome>
        <ways><tradition>6</tradition></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_YearOfTheDead</thought><exceptTrait><li>Psychopath</li></exceptTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>-2</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>The year of the muffalo</label>
        <outcome>It is the year of the muffalo. The muffalo has not been told. {A_nameDef} is sulking.</outcome>
        <ways><tradition>-3</tradition></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Muffalo</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>-3</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

  <!-- ===================== The spoils ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Council_Dilemma_Spoils</defName>
    <label>the spoils</label>
    <weight>1</weight>
    <cooldownDays>20</cooldownDays>
    <withinDaysOfThreat>2</withinDaysOfThreat>
    <roleA>
      <canFight>true</canFight>
      <bestAt>Shooting</bestAt>
    </roleA>
    <texts>
      <li>The raiders left plenty behind: boots, coats, a weapon or two still in good shape. {A_nameDef} did most of the shooting and thinks that earns {A_objective} first pick.\n\nSome of the others disagree.</li>
      <li>The bodies are still warm, and the argument over their gear has already started. {A_nameDef}, who killed three of them, has claimed the best of it.</li>
    </texts>
    <defaultOption>1</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>{A_nameDef} earned first pick</label>
        <outcome>{A_nameDef} took the best of the spoils. A few of the others grumble that they fought too.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>-4</generosity></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_Dlm_FirstPick</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>5</amount></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_Dlm_SpoilsUnfair</thought><onlyTrait><li>Greedy</li><li>Jealous</li></onlyTrait></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Share everything equally</label>
        <outcome>The spoils went to the common stores, to be shared out equally. Most think that's fair. {A_nameDef} doesn't, and says so.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>4</generosity></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_Dlm_FairShares</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>-3</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>The fighters get the spoils</label>
        <outcome>Everyone who fought got a share. Those who stayed inside got nothing but the cleanup, and some of them resent it.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>-2</generosity><tradition>2</tradition></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_Dlm_FairShares</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_Dlm_SpoilsUnfair</thought><onlyTrait><li>Wimp</li><li>Kind</li></onlyTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>3</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

  <!-- ===================== The enemy dead ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Council_Dilemma_EnemyDead</defName>
    <label>the enemy dead</label>
    <weight>1</weight>
    <cooldownDays>20</cooldownDays>
    <withinDaysOfThreat>2</withinDaysOfThreat>
    <texts>
      <li>The raiders lie where they fell. {A_nameDef} asks what the council wants done with them: graves, a pyre, or the treeline and the scavengers.\n\nThe colony is divided on it, and loudly.</li>
      <li>{A_nameDef} has been standing over the bodies outside the wall since the fighting stopped. "They were people," {A_nameDef} says. "Somebody's people. What do we do with them?"</li>
    </texts>
    <traditionOption>0</traditionOption>
    <traditionLabel>burying the enemy dead</traditionLabel>
    <defaultOption>2</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>Give them graves</label>
        <outcome>The raiders were buried outside the colony, which took most of a day. Some colonists slept better for it; others resent the work.</outcome>
        <ways><mercy>6</mercy><tradition>3</tradition></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_DecentBurial</thought><onlyTrait><li>Kind</li></onlyTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Unfair</thought><onlyTrait><li>Bloodlust</li><li>Abrasive</li></onlyTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>3</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Burn them</label>
        <outcome>The bodies were burned on a pyre that went all night. The smell hung over the colony until morning.</outcome>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Pyre</thought><onlyTrait><li>Pyromaniac</li></onlyTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Harsh</thought><onlyTrait><li>Kind</li></onlyTrait></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Drag them to the treeline</label>
        <outcome>The bodies were dragged to the treeline. The scavengers came at dusk, and they could be heard from inside the walls.</outcome>
        <ways><mercy>-6</mercy></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_BodiesLeft</thought><exceptTrait><li>Psychopath</li><li>Bloodlust</li></exceptTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_FairsFair</thought><onlyTrait><li>Bloodlust</li></onlyTrait></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

  <!-- ===================== Victory feast ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Council_Dilemma_VictoryFeast</defName>
    <label>after the battle</label>
    <workerClass>ColonyCouncil.DilemmaWorker_Feast</workerClass>
    <weight>0.8</weight>
    <cooldownDays>25</cooldownDays>
    <withinDaysOfThreat>1.5</withinDaysOfThreat>
    <thingCount>20</thingCount>
    <texts>
      <li>The colony has come through the attack, and the survivors are giddy with it. {A_nameDef} wants to celebrate properly with a victory feast tonight, using about {COUNT} raw food.\n\nThe repairs would have to wait until morning.</li>
      <li>The fighting stopped an hour ago, and {A_nameDef} is already asking the council for a feast. "We earned it," {A_nameDef} says, wiping someone else's blood off {A_possessive} sleeve.</li>
    </texts>
    <traditionOption>0</traditionOption>
    <traditionLabel>the victory feast</traditionLabel>
    <defaultOption>1</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>A victory feast</label>
        <outcome>They ate and drank until well after dark, loud with relief.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>3</generosity><toil>-5</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Consume"><what>rawfood</what></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_VictoryFeast</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>Colony</target><amount>2</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Repairs first, celebrations later</label>
        <outcome>It was straight back to work on the walls, the wounded and the bodies. The celebration never happened.</outcome>
        <ways><toil>6</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_NoCelebration</thought><exceptTrait><li>Ascetic</li></exceptTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_Dlm_FairsFair</thought><degreeTrait>Industriousness</degreeTrait><minDegree>1</minDegree></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

</Defs>
